=== ROOT CAUSE ANALYSIS ===

1. APPLICATION ROUTES MISSING (7 of 8 services)
   - All services except telegram-bridge return Flask 404 on every tested path
     (/, /healthz, /plan, /allowlist, /dashboard/*, /health-check, etc.).
   - The Flask dev server IS running (distinctive werkzeug 404 HTML vs Google
     GFE 404). The services are not crashing — they just have zero or near-zero
     routes defined in their deployed images.
   - Likely cause: The Docker images were built from earlier scaffolding code
     that had minimal Flask templates without the route definitions present
     in the current source code. The images need to be rebuilt and redeployed
     from the current track-a/main.py, track-b/main.py, and agent source files.

2. /healthz INTERCEPTED BY CLOUD RUN GFE (all 8 services)
   - Even telegram-bridge (which has working routes) returns a Google-styled
     404 on /healthz — different from the Flask 404 on other missing routes.
   - This indicates the Cloud Run Google Front End (GFE) is intercepting
     requests to /healthz before they reach the container.
   - Recommendation: Use an alternative health check path (e.g., /health,
     /ping, or use the root / endpoint) or configure Cloud Run's health
     check probe to use a TCP check instead of HTTP path-based check.

3. EIM WEB UI — DNS NOT CONFIGURED
   - The domain cem.ai-staffing-solutions-consultants.online does not resolve.
   - Requires: domain registration + DNS records pointing to Cloudflare Pages
     or the target hosting platform.

